    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The mid-day sun NEVER shines overhead on any latitude beyond the Tropic of Cancer and the Tropic of Capricorn.",
        "Areas lying between the Arctic Circle and the North Pole in the Northern Hemisphere are called the Frigid Zone because the sun does not rise much above the horizon.",
        "Maximum solar radiation (insolation) is received in the Torrid Zone due to direct vertical sun rays."
      ],
      "id": "dksbb1o"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Torrid Zone lies between the Tropic of Cancer (23½° N) and the Tropic of Capricorn (23½° S) and receives the maximum heat.",
        "The Temperate Zones lie between the Tropics and the Polar Circles in both hemispheres and experience moderate temperatures.",
        "The Frigid Zones are located between the Arctic/Antarctic Circles and the Poles, receiving highly slanting sun rays resulting in extreme cold.",
        "The angle of the sun's rays decreases continuously from the Equator towards the Poles."
      ],
      "id": "5gj50be"
    }
